{"definition":"To perish, be destroyed, or cause something to be lost or wiped out — covering loss, ruin, and destruction across a wide range.","senseLabels":["Perish / be destroyed","Cause to destroy / wipe out","Be lost / ruined"],"article":"אָבַד covers the full arc from something quietly disappearing to violent, total destruction. In the Qal stem it most often means to perish or be lost; the Piel and Hiphil stems push the meaning toward actively causing ruin. Its 185 occurrences span 25 books, with the heaviest use in Jeremiah, Psalms, and Deuteronomy — both poetic lament and covenantal warning. The LXX translators chose ἀπόλλυμι an overwhelming 118 times, the very Greek root later used for 'destruction' and 'the destroyer' in the New Testament.","caution":null}
